# What an image build must never see.
#
# The first entries are not about size. A build context is handed to the daemon
# whole before any instruction runs, and the builder stage does `COPY . .`, so
# anything matching these patterns would reach a layer. A certificate tool
# baking private key material into an image is the specific failure this
# prevents — and it is the one failure here that cannot be undone by deleting
# the image, because layers get pushed.
.env
.env.*
.certpilot/
*.pem
*.key
config.dev.yaml

# Not inputs to the binary.
.git/
.github/
bin/
*.md
*.log
.DS_Store
